1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,609
WebMCP makes a website callable by agents. WorkHub Goal Room makes each call state-aware, authority-checked, evidence-bound, and owner-controlled.

2
00:00:07,729 --> 00:00:24,216
Here is the native boundary first. Canary returned six browser-native RegisteredTool descriptors. The Agent path is getTools, select the browser-returned tool, then executeTool with serialized JSON. There is no tool for Owner decisions, System verdicts, acceptance, or external effects.

3
00:00:24,336 --> 00:00:34,481
The static registration list follows source order. This panel preserves the raw browser enumeration separately. No model autonomously selected a tool in this evidence.

4
00:00:34,601 --> 00:00:45,169
A malformed call can be rejected without changing state or receipts. The recorded S fourteen probe proves malformed-input atomicity, not a schema-valid terminal reducer refusal.

5
00:00:45,289 --> 00:00:57,971
The journey starts with owner intent. The Agent proposes Goal Contract version one. The Owner asks for a revision, the Agent proposes version two, and only the Owner confirms it.

6
00:00:58,091 --> 00:01:10,773
The same boundary applies to planning. Plan version one is revised. Plan version two remains bound to confirmed Goal Contract version two, and the Owner confirms it before work begins.

7
00:01:10,893 --> 00:01:26,111
The Agent claims the admitted step and submits Candidate version one. The production System adapter runs the deterministic rule set automatically and records FAIL. System verdict authorship is neither an Agent tool nor an Owner control.

8
00:01:26,231 --> 00:01:39,336
The Agent corrects the evidence and submits Candidate version two. The same rules record PASS for the exact candidate version and SHA two fifty-six. The next actor is still the Agent.

9
00:01:39,456 --> 00:01:46,642
PASS does not mean accepted. PASS only permits the Agent to request completion for that exact candidate.

10
00:01:46,762 --> 00:01:58,599
After the request, the Owner sees Candidate version two, its full digest, the rule-set version, PASS, and the irreversible consequence. Only this trusted Owner interface can confirm acceptance.

11
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:06,751
S fourteen is sealed. The current actor is none, there are no controls, and there is no legal continuation.

12
00:02:06,871 --> 00:02:18,707
The mobile projection keeps the same frontier, while the eleven ninety-nine and twelve hundred pixel captures prove which one of the two compositions is active at the boundary.

13
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:33,200
This competition edition is one synthetic browser-local Goal. It has no accounts, backend persistence, cloud service, database, external effects, or autonomous-model reliability claim. Public app, repository, YouTube, and Devpost actions remain pending Owner approval.
